@lang en
IMPORT `homecare-part2`

-- Liberty HomeCare (UW-RPP-W-001-06-V), Part 1, Material Damage (PHẦN 1 – THIỆT HẠI VẬT
-- CHẤT): the insuring clause, the basis of settlement, Provisions 1-3, Pairs and Sets, the
-- General Limit of Liability, Proof of Value (a duty, in homecare-general-conditions.l4),
-- Extensions 1-7 and Exclusions 1-8. Quotations (`src:N`) are line N of
-- ../../source/raw/liberty-homecare.txt.
--
-- LAYER 1 (is the loss covered?) is `the grounds on which a Part 1 claim fails`; an empty
-- list means covered. LAYER 2 (how much?) is `Part 1: the amount payable`, which applies the
-- settlement basis, the Provisions, Pairs and Sets, GC6, the General Limit, GC9 and, last,
-- the GC13 Deductible (F-order). Layer 3 (duties) is in homecare-general-conditions.l4.

§ `Part 1. Material Damage`

DECLARE `A ground under Part 1` IS ONE OF
    `Introduction: cover had not attached`
    `the item claimed is not insured under Part 1`
    `the property is not within the definition of the item claimed`
    `no sudden and unforeseen physical loss, destruction or damage`
    `the loss was not in the Period of Insurance`
    `the loss was not at the Insured Location`
    `an Insured Peril ground` HAS `which` IS A `A ground under the Insured Perils`
    `Part 1 exclusion 1: scratching, denting, chipping or marring`
    `Part 1 exclusion 2: wear and tear, gradual causes, light or atmosphere, pests`
    `Part 1 exclusion 3: electrical or electronic breakdown, or a manufacturing or design defect`
    `Part 1 exclusion 4: consequential loss`
    `Part 1 exclusion 5: unexplained loss or mysterious disappearance`
    `Part 1 exclusion 6: programming, labelling or data errors`
    `Part 1 exclusion 7: pollution or contamination`
    `Part 1 exclusion 8: property more specifically insured`
    `a General Exclusion` HAS `which` IS A `A General Exclusion`
    `a General Condition` HAS `which` IS A `A ground under the General Conditions`

§§ `Scope of cover`

-- Where insured property (the Home, the Renovation Costs, the Contents) suffers sudden and
-- unforeseen physical loss, destruction or damage in the Period of Insurance at the Insured
-- Location, caused by an Insured Peril, the Insurer will at its option reinstate, replace or
-- repair it, up to the sum insured or Limit of Liability in the Policy Summary.
