GIVEN loss IS A `A Part 1 loss`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A ground under Part 1`
`Part 1 exclusions 1 to 8 that apply to` loss MEANS
    `those that hold among`
        (LIST PAIR `Part 1 exclusion 1: scratching, denting, chipping or marring`
                   (`it was` `scratching, denting, chipping or marring only`)
            , PAIR `Part 1 exclusion 2: wear and tear, gradual causes, light or atmosphere, pests`
                   (   `it was` `wear and tear or depreciation`
                    OR `it was` `cleaning, dyeing, alteration, repair or restoration`
                    OR `it was` `the action of light or atmospheric conditions`
                    OR `it was` `rot, mildew, rust, moths, insects or vermin`
                    OR `it was` `any other gradually operating cause`)
            , PAIR `Part 1 exclusion 3: electrical or electronic breakdown, or a manufacturing or design defect`
                   (   `it was` `electrical or electronic breakdown or failure to operate`
                    OR `it was` `a manufacturer's defect or design defect`)
            , PAIR `Part 1 exclusion 4: consequential loss` (`it was` `the loss claimed is consequential or indirect`)
            , PAIR `Part 1 exclusion 5: unexplained loss or mysterious disappearance` (`it was` `unexplained loss or mysterious disappearance`)
            , PAIR `Part 1 exclusion 6: programming, labelling or data errors` (`it was` `errors of programming, punching, labelling or insertion, or loss of data`)
            , PAIR `Part 1 exclusion 7: pollution or contamination`
                   (    `it was` `pollution or contamination`
                    AND NOT "(a)" ... `it was` `the pollution or contamination was caused by an insured peril`
                    AND NOT "(b)" ... `it was` `an insured peril was caused by pollution or contamination`)
            , PAIR `Part 1 exclusion 8: property more specifically insured` (`it was` `the property is more specifically insured by or for the Insured`))
    WHERE
        `it was` c MEANS elem c (loss's `the circumstances`)

§§ `Basis of settlement and Provisions 1-3`

-- (a) Where property is lost or destroyed: for the Home, the cost of rebuilding; for other
-- property, the cost of replacing it with similar property; in either case to a condition
-- equal to but not better or more extensive than when new. (b) Where property is damaged: the
-- cost of repairing the damage and restoring the damaged part to a condition equal to but not
-- better or more extensive than when new. That cost is the input `the cost of reinstatement`
-- (the adjuster's figure on this basis): the basis is new for old, without deduction.
