`Extension 2: the share of the sum insured` MEANS 5%

@ref Part 1, Extension 2, src:348-354
GIVEN `the claim for this loss` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum insured on the item` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Extension 2: no inventory of undamaged property is needed for a claim of` `the claim for this loss` `on an item insured for` `the sum insured on the item` MEANS
    `the claim for this loss` AT MOST
        min `Extension 2: the fixed threshold, in dong`
            (`Extension 2: the share of the sum insured` TIMES `the sum insured on the item`)

-- 3. Architects', surveyors' and consulting engineers' fees, legal and other fees for
-- estimates, plans, specifications, quantities, tenders and supervision reasonably incurred
-- in reinstating the damage are part of the Home cover, not the costs of preparing a claim;
-- no more than the scales of the professional bodies allow, and in all no more than 10% of
-- the total sum insured on the Home. Input convention: the fees given exclude claim
-- preparation.
