-- 4. Fire fighting: costs necessarily and reasonably incurred in extinguishing a fire at or
-- near insured property or threatening it, or preventing imminent damage by any insured
-- peril, including damage done to reach the fire; no more than 10% of "the sum insured under
-- this Part". F-ext-base: that is the total sum insured under Part 1.
